Description:

Synopsis:
Elevate customers require payment billing files to update their own systems and LNET system should generate billing files that include all items reported under a TAR job. The system should ensure the file structure aligns with each clients' specifications.

As a loan servicing user on the TAR Disbursements tab, I want to export a billing file for customers 1072, 2118, 2215, 2161, and 2164, so that each customer receives a .txt file in their required layout containing all reported TAR job items.

Background
These five customers share the same base query as Pattern 1 (Loan Number, Tax ID, Amount to Pay, ELD date) but additionally require payee/agency resolution logic - the file must conditionally output either an AgencyNumber or a PayeeCode depending on a per-customer configuration flag. Customers
2161 and 2164 further require a Michigan county code prefix in Elevate was derived from the payee code, which in the original DTSX was an 83-branch CASE statement. This story needs to replace that as PayeeCode does not exist in LeretaNet.

In Scope:

