## 4. BillingFileFormatter.cs — Minor Fix

**File:** `LeretanetCore/LeretanetCore.Web/Utility/BillingFileFormatter.cs`

Customer 1072 returns `NULL` for `AmtToPay` when `InstallmentInd` is outside 1–4. The existing `ApplyTransform` method attempts to parse the value for the `CENTS` transform, which throws on an empty/null input. Add a null guard at the top of `ApplyTransform`:

```csharp
private static string ApplyTransform(string value, string transform)
{
    if (string.IsNullOrEmpty(value)) return value;  // null/empty passes through unchanged
    // ... existing CENTS, MMDDYY logic unchanged
}
```

When `AmtToPay` is null, the formatter will output `value = ""` which after `PadLeft(10)` produces 10 spaces — matching the expected blank amount field.

